 "description": "BIGVILLE R22b (block 272000) -- INFANT MORTALITY: well-baby care drops infant mortality, the SHARPEST inequality face. Three rules apply R22's preventive/public machinery to a HIGH-FRAGILITY R14 infant life stage. bi_onset computes the effective acute drop D = max(0, disease_base + (well_baby?0:infant_fragility)) -- an UNSEEN infant takes the fragility penalty and can die of a shock an adult (or a seen baby) survives; a baby under regular well-baby care (well_baby=1) takes the base drop only. bi_wellbaby (PRIVATE, out-of-pocket, affordability-gated -- the poor can't afford regular visits -> their infants die -> infant mortality TRACKS wealth) and bi_wellbaby_public (COUNCIL-FUNDED, treasury pays, R9 shape -- the STRUCTURAL LEVER that dissolves the wealth-infant-mortality gradient). The fee is a CONSERVED coin transfer; affordability is the where Gte gate. well_baby removes the fragility penalty exactly as R22's screened removes progression. Matches its OWN arm (infant_disease_armed) + guards infant==1 so R22's bd_onset (disease_armed) is never double-fired. NO reward/punishment token (illness/death are STATES; the RESTORE is well-baby care / public provision). Composes existing DSL Terms; ZERO new Rust. The infant-mortality lever is the demographic-transition driver R23 needs.",
